# 08 — Loudspeaker

The loudspeaker is driven through the phone's audio DSP. The microphone
and the earpiece aren't supported by the kernel yet.

## Route audio to the loudspeaker

`ExAudio` sets ALSA mixer controls. At boot the firmware already enables
this route for the Fairphone 3+; running it again is harmless.

```elixir
ExAudio.cset("QUIN_MI2S_RX Audio Mixer MultiMedia1", :on)
```

On a Fairphone 3+ the amplifier also has an on/off switch (the Fairphone
3 amplifier doesn't, so this returns an error there):

```elixir
ExAudio.cset("Speaker Switch", :on)
```

## Play a tone

Generate one second of a 440 Hz tone, save it as a WAV file and play it
with `aplay`.

```elixir
rate = 48_000
volume = 0.3

tone =
  Nx.iota({rate}, type: :f32)
  |> Nx.multiply(2 * :math.pi() * 440 / rate)
  |> Nx.sin()
  |> Nx.multiply(volume)

InferAudio.Decoder.write_wav("/tmp/tone.wav", tone, sample_rate: rate)
System.cmd("aplay", ["-D", "plughw:0,0", "/tmp/tone.wav"], stderr_to_stdout: true)
```

Change `volume` (0.0 to 1.0) and run it again.

## A short melody

```elixir
notes = [262, 294, 330, 349, 392, 440, 494, 523]

melody =
  for freq <- notes do
    Nx.iota({div(rate, 4)}, type: :f32)
    |> Nx.multiply(2 * :math.pi() * freq / rate)
    |> Nx.sin()
    |> Nx.multiply(volume)
  end
  |> Nx.concatenate()

InferAudio.Decoder.write_wav("/tmp/melody.wav", melody, sample_rate: rate)
System.cmd("aplay", ["-D", "plughw:0,0", "/tmp/melody.wav"], stderr_to_stdout: true)
```

## Play your own file

`aplay` plays WAV files. Copy one to the phone (for example with
`sftp nerves.local`) and play it:

```elixir
System.cmd("aplay", ["-D", "plughw:0,0", "/data/my_sound.wav"], stderr_to_stdout: true)
```
